@startuml Declaration Lifecycle

title Declaration lifecycle (GMR, ENS, ELO, Ukrainian goods list)
caption Target design. Customs declarations: Lifecycle. Decisions X5, X6, D13, X2. ADRs 0005, 0006.

state "Draft" as Draft : being prepared
state "Ready to file" as Ready : snapshot of the load stored
state "Filed" as Filed : submitted, or recorded as filed
state "Accepted" as Accepted : authority issued a reference;\nthe only "current" state
state "Refused" as Refused : bounded reason code only
state "Stale" as Stale : load differs from the snapshot;\nderived, never set by hand
state "Withdrawn" as Withdrawn : cancelled or invalidated;\nrecord and reference kept
state "Closed" as Closed : its border has been crossed;\nfrozen

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : load signed off,\nsnapshot taken
Ready --> Filed : filed (automatic)\nor reference recorded (manual)
Filed --> Accepted : authority accepts
Filed --> Refused : authority refuses
Refused --> Draft : corrected
Filed --> Stale : load changed
Accepted --> Stale : load changed
Stale --> Withdrawn : withdraw (re-declare task)
Withdrawn --> Draft : replacement started\nfor the same scope
Accepted --> Closed : Convoy Leader (or Dispatcher\non their behalf) marks the crossing
Closed --> [*]

note right of Filed
  ENS: Filed and Accepted collapse,
  because an MRN exists only on acceptance.
  ELO: needs an Accepted ENS first.
end note

note left of Stale
  Stale while the convoy is planned
  blocks departure.
end note

@enduml
